WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.659 --> 00:00:02.869
(jazzy music)

00:00:02.869 --> 00:00:05.536
(train running)

00:00:06.584 --> 00:00:09.917
- [Philip] The idea came from my father.

00:00:10.833 --> 00:00:14.022
He told me that there
are pictures on the walls

00:00:14.022 --> 00:00:18.841
and the subway stations of
old buildings, you know, old New York.

00:00:18.841 --> 00:00:20.850
(train running)

00:00:20.850 --> 00:00:22.475
20 years later, after
going through everything,

00:00:22.475 --> 00:00:24.310
school, college and all that stuff,

00:00:24.310 --> 00:00:25.508
I thought I would finally give it a look

00:00:25.508 --> 00:00:29.827
and to see what my
father was talking about.

00:00:29.827 --> 00:00:32.187
It was gonna be a short article.

00:00:32.187 --> 00:00:33.859
I was going to illustrate some stations

00:00:33.859 --> 00:00:37.478
with some pictures and tell the stories.

00:00:37.478 --> 00:00:38.614
(laughs)

00:00:38.614 --> 00:00:41.114
But it kinda ran away with me.

00:00:46.389 --> 00:00:49.139
(subway running)

00:00:52.379 --> 00:00:54.464
What I set out to do is make a record

00:00:54.464 --> 00:00:58.631
of the appearance of the subway
stations in New York City.

00:00:59.549 --> 00:01:03.062
I take drawings of the
mosaic or faience designs

00:01:03.062 --> 00:01:06.267
on the walls which embellish the stations.

00:01:06.267 --> 00:01:08.809
(atmospheric music)

00:01:08.809 --> 00:01:11.654
I devote as much of my
time as I can to doing it.

00:01:11.654 --> 00:01:15.276
Evenings, weekends, vacation time even,

00:01:15.276 --> 00:01:18.859
you know, it's sort of
a consuming project.

00:01:20.326 --> 00:01:22.950
(upbeat music)

00:01:22.950 --> 00:01:25.748
So far, I've completed four volumes,

00:01:25.748 --> 00:01:28.415
volume one, two, three and four.

00:01:30.044 --> 00:01:32.006
My ambition is to take
care of all the lines

00:01:32.006 --> 00:01:33.756
until all 496 or 469,

00:01:39.552 --> 00:01:42.969
470 stations have been recorded and seen.

00:01:46.809 --> 00:01:48.306
Why am I doing it?

00:01:48.306 --> 00:01:49.607
(laughs)

00:01:49.607 --> 00:01:53.937
Okay, my purpose in doing
this study is to make

00:01:53.937 --> 00:01:56.187
a record of what we've got.

00:01:57.153 --> 00:01:59.656
I wanted to like,
document when it was done

00:01:59.656 --> 00:02:00.906
and who did it.

00:02:02.071 --> 00:02:03.371
So that's what I wanted to do.

00:02:03.371 --> 00:02:05.647
That's my focus, is to
give credit to those

00:02:05.647 --> 00:02:07.397
who made it possible.

00:02:08.584 --> 00:02:11.626
(subway announcement)

00:02:11.626 --> 00:02:14.714
I really started in earnest in 1978.

00:02:14.714 --> 00:02:17.628
And I thought I'd get this
project finished and wrapped up

00:02:17.628 --> 00:02:21.795
by the year 2030, which
is only 14 years from now.

00:02:23.050 --> 00:02:27.427
Perhaps I have to
re-estimate and, uh, suggest maybe

00:02:27.427 --> 00:02:28.677
closer to 2040.

00:02:34.091 --> 00:02:36.424
I'll be in my nineties then.

00:02:37.609 --> 00:02:38.817
I hope I can still see.

00:02:38.817 --> 00:02:40.900
(laughs)

00:02:42.404 --> 00:02:45.821
The pleasure of doing the job is, um, payment.

00:02:47.362 --> 00:02:48.952
I've committed to it, that's all.

00:02:48.952 --> 00:02:50.287
It's my purpose.

00:02:50.287 --> 00:02:51.414
It's my life.

00:02:51.414 --> 00:02:53.414
It's become my identity.

00:02:54.873 --> 00:02:57.123
So I have to live up to it.

00:02:58.089 --> 00:03:00.756
(train running)

